# Park Rules Overview

This section outlines the rules and regulations that visitors must follow while enjoying the facilities at AeroSports Scarborough, including requirements for socks, spectator policies, toddler supervision, weight limits on trampolines, waiver procedures, refund policies, pricing details, go-karting guidelines, child supervision, food restrictions, Wi-Fi availability, hiring age, and gift card information.

[3] (source: location_info.md)
## Useful Links

For booking activities or parties, visit the main booking page at https://ecom.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/products/en/home. If you are interested in organizing a birthday party, use this specific link: https://ecom.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/birthdayparties/en/products. To access and complete necessary waivers, go to https://waiver.roller.app/aerosportsscarborough/. For directions or to view the location on Google Maps, visit https://g.page/AeroSports-scarborough. Birthday invitations can be created at https://aerosportsinvitation.netlify.app/invitationscarborough.

[4] (source: jump_prices.md)
### Open Jump Passes

AeroSports Scarborough offers various open jump passes tailored to different age groups and preferences.

- **Premium Jump Pass**: For guests aged six years and older, the Premium Jump Pass costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents for ninety minutes. This pass grants access to all attractions except Go Karting, Laser Tag, Bazooka Ball, and Mini Golf.
  
- **VIP Jump Pass**: Also available for guests aged six years and older, the VIP Jump Pass is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents for a duration of one hundred and twenty minutes. Similar to the Premium Jump Pass, it includes access to all attractions except Go Karting, Laser Tag, Bazooka Ball, and Mini Golf.

- **Premium Jump Pass for Ages 2 to 5**: Children aged two to five can enjoy the same benefits as older guests with this pass, which costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents for ninety minutes. It includes access to all attractions except Go Karting, Laser Tag, Bazooka Ball, and Mini Golf.

- **VIP Jump Pass for Ages 2 to 5**: This pass is available for children aged two to five at a cost of twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred and twenty minutes. It provides the same access as the VIP Jump Pass for older guests.

- **Ultimate Jump Pass**: Designed for guests aged six years and older, the Ultimate Jump Pass costs forty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred and eighty minutes. This pass includes access to all core attractions, with the option to choose between Go Karting or Mini Golf and Laser Tag or Bazooka Ball.

- **Passes for Children Under 2**: Any jump pass is free for children under two years old, provided they are accompanied by a paying adult. The duration matches that of the accompanying adult's pass.

- **All Day Pass**: Available to all guests, the All Day Jump Pass costs thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents and allows unlimited access to attractions throughout the day.

[5] (source: attractions.md)
## Go Karting Thrills

Indoor go-kart racing at AeroSports Scarborough features two tracks: a Main Track designed for taller riders and a Mini Track suitable for younger children. The electric karts allow up to ten laps per race.

- **Age/Height Requirements:** For the Main Track, participants must be at least fifty-two inches tall. For the Mini Track, they must be at least thirty-six inches tall. Closed-toed shoes are required.
- **Included in Jump Pass:** No
- **Pricing Details:** Go-karting requires a separate ticket or can be added as an add-on to your visit. Pricing details can be found on the dedicated Go Karting sheet.

[6] (source: attractions.md)
## Rock Walls Adventure

The indoor rock climbing walls at AeroSports Scarborough present various difficulty levels, allowing participants to test their strength and push their limits as they climb to the top.

- **Age/Height Requirements:** Open to all ages.
- **Included in Jump Pass:** Yes
- **Pricing Details:** Access to the Rock Walls is included with any jump pass, making it an attractive option for climbers of all skill levels.

[7] (source: attractions.md)
## Jump Tower / Aero Drop

The Jump Tower/Aero Drop attraction at AeroSports Scarborough provides an adrenaline-filled free-fall jump from above. Participants leap off the tower and land safely below, making it ideal for thrill seekers.

- **Age/Height Requirements:** Open to all ages.
- **Included in Jump Pass:** Yes
- **Pricing Details:** This thrilling experience is included with any jump pass, ensuring everyone can enjoy the excitement of free-falling.


